WEBVTT

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.880
Assured mission partner
collaboration is critical for

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.620
operational success.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.800
Mattermost simplifies complex
operations through unified

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.340
workflows with
decision advantage.

00:00:17.015 --> 00:00:19.575
This demo highlights how
federated workspaces,

00:00:19.575 --> 00:00:22.455
external data feeds and
interoperability with matrix or

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.935
other legacy systems come
together in Mattermost.

00:00:24.935 --> 00:00:26.135
With AI tools,

00:00:26.135 --> 00:00:29.650
auto translation and
integrated Pexip video calls,

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:32.530
you'll see how decisions
are accelerated and mission

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.290
objectives are achieved.

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:37.710
Let's put this into action
with a simulated scenario.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:42.850
Major Alex Reyes, an operations
officer at the joint forward

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.415
element is monitoring the Indo
Pacific theater for potential

00:00:46.415 --> 00:00:49.615
threats and leading the
allied team's rapid response

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:51.215
coordination efforts.

00:00:51.215 --> 00:00:52.975
In the intel watch channel,

00:00:52.975 --> 00:00:55.775
which is governed by
attribute based access,

00:00:55.775 --> 00:01:00.180
alerts begin to flow from ISR
analysts and cyber defense teams.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.400
Airborne ISR collection over
Okinawa shows anomalies.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:09.540
Additionally, cyber defense units
flag intrusion attempts targeting

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.520
SATCOM ground stations.

00:01:11.795 --> 00:01:12.915
Behind the scenes,

00:01:12.915 --> 00:01:16.275
external threat intelligence
systems enrich alert data using

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:17.555
tip and cue methods,

00:01:17.555 --> 00:01:20.915
while Mattermost connects the teams
to act on the insights.

00:01:20.915 --> 00:01:25.555
Once confirmed, key intelligence is
escalated with allies in the Indo Pacific

00:01:25.555 --> 00:01:27.750
response ops shared channel.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:31.470
Reyes posts a summary of the
threat indicators to initiate

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:32.750
the joint response,

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:36.510
and allied teams immediately
begin synthesizing context

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:40.010
rapidly aligning on a
coordinated course of action.

00:01:40.495 --> 00:01:44.415
The Indo Pacific response ops
channel provides a synchronized

00:01:44.415 --> 00:01:47.535
space where mission partners
coordinate securely across

00:01:47.535 --> 00:01:49.355
organizational boundaries.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:52.320
Each team retains control
of its own enclave,

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.380
but shared situational threads
flow seamlessly between partners.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.840
Mattermost's auto
translation ensures fast,

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.760
accurate comprehension across
Japanese and English speaking teams.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.075
As messages flow into
the shared channel,

00:02:06.075 --> 00:02:09.595
Japan defense and joint forward
element personnel view native

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:11.435
language versions instantly,

00:02:11.435 --> 00:02:15.335
preserving speed and clarity during
early stage threat coordination.

00:02:16.475 --> 00:02:19.830
Major Reyes initiates the
multi domain threat response protocol

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.750
using a Mattermost playbook,

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.870
automating key coordination
steps across intelligence,

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.090
cyber and air
response functions.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:31.445
Mattermost playbooks ensure
a structured response,

00:02:31.445 --> 00:02:32.965
Standardizing workflows,

00:02:32.965 --> 00:02:36.565
assigning roles and preserving
audit trails even under time

00:02:36.565 --> 00:02:38.065
critical conditions.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.400
Leaders convene securely
using the Mattermost Pexip

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:53.100
integration enabling sovereign
IL5 compliant video conferencing.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.600
A live call is launched
directly from the Indo Pacific

00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:00.245
response ops channel where ISR
imagery is reviewed in real time.

00:03:01.865 --> 00:03:04.825
A forward deployed detachment
lead maintains critical

00:03:04.825 --> 00:03:08.805
connectivity using a field kit
designed for degraded environments.

00:03:11.465 --> 00:03:14.760
The expeditionary setup enables
mission critical updates to

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.080
flow through the shared
coordination channel,

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.960
ensuring real time alignment
with partner forces at Joint

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:23.860
Forward Element, Japan Defense,
and across the theater.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.585
Major Reyes uses a
slash command to retrieve high

00:03:28.585 --> 00:03:31.125
resolution imagery
from a drone asset.

00:03:37.385 --> 00:03:40.645
A Japan defense analyst
overlays risk zones.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:46.720
As allied teams rotate in
and out of the mission,

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:51.100
a partner analyst joins Indo
Pacific response ops mid operation.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:55.375
Major Reyes uses Mattermost AI
agents backed with a sovereign

00:03:55.375 --> 00:03:58.415
government grade LLM providing
the partner analyst with a

00:03:58.415 --> 00:04:02.875
concise update on ISR trends
and task force actions so far.

00:04:03.295 --> 00:04:07.595
With the ability to integrate
with systems like Matrix or XMPP,

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:11.030
partner forces leaders
remain situationally aware as

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:13.750
information flows across
partners who may still be

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:16.050
operating within legacy systems.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:19.190
Here, we can see a Matrix room
synced with a shared channel in

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.405
Mattermost for allied comms.

00:04:21.685 --> 00:04:25.045
From intel to action, every
task has been executed.

00:04:25.045 --> 00:04:27.845
The response playbook is
complete and a final status

00:04:27.845 --> 00:04:31.265
update thanks all partners for
securing the region together.

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:35.530
At the center of a
mission ready network,

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:37.770
Mattermost bridges
partners, platforms,

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:40.730
and intelligence to deliver
decision advantage in multi

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:44.710
domain operations, all grounded
in zero trust principles.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:50.735
From signal to decision,
Mattermost keeps the mission in

00:04:55.701 --> 00:04:56.801
motion.